### Complete Starkvault Workflow Test
### This file demonstrates a complete user workflow from signup to file management

### Base URL
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000

### Test User Data
@workflowEmail = workflow@example.com
@workflowPassword = workflow123
@workflowName = Workflow Test User

###
### STEP 1: Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health

###
### STEP 2: Create New User Account
# @name signup
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{workflowName}}",
  "email": "{{workflowEmail}}",
  "password": "{{workflowPassword}}"
}

###
### STEP 3: Login to Get Authentication Cookie
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{workflowEmail}}",
  "password": "{{workflowPassword}}"
}

###
### STEP 4: Verify Authentication - Get Current User
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me

###
### STEP 5: Upload First Document
# @name uploadDoc1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=workflow1

--workflow1
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="important-contract.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

IMPORTANT CONTRACT DOCUMENT

This is a sample contract document that demonstrates the permanent storage capabilities of Arweave through the Starkvault platform.

Contract Details:
- Date: 2026-02-05
- Parties: Company A and Company B
- Terms: Standard service agreement
- Duration: 12 months

This document will be permanently stored on the Arweave blockchain and cannot be deleted or modified once uploaded.
--workflow1
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Important business contract requiring permanent storage
--workflow1
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

contract,business,important,legal,permanent
--workflow1
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="isPublic"

false
--workflow1--

###
### STEP 6: Upload Second Document (Public)
# @name uploadDoc2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=workflow2

--workflow2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="public-announcement.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

PUBLIC ANNOUNCEMENT

This is a public announcement document that can be shared with others.

Announcement Details:
- Company: Starkvault Inc.
- Date: 2026-02-05
- Subject: New Arweave Integration Launch

We are excited to announce the launch of our new Arweave integration for permanent document storage!
--workflow2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Public company announcement about Arweave integration
--workflow2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="tags"

announcement,public,company,arweave,launch
--workflow2
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="isPublic"

true
--workflow2--

###
### STEP 7: List All Documents
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents

###
### STEP 8: Search Documents by Tag
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents?search=contract

###
### STEP 9: Search Documents by Description
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents?search=announcement

###
### STEP 10: Get Specific Document Details
### Note: Replace with actual document ID from upload response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/document/REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_DOCUMENT_ID

###
### STEP 11: Check Arweave Transaction Status
### Note: Replace with actual Arweave hash from upload response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/status/REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_ARWEAVE_HASH

###
### STEP 12: Download File from Arweave
### Note: Replace with actual Arweave hash from upload response
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file/REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_ARWEAVE_HASH

###
### STEP 13: Upload Document with Validation Errors (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/file
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=workflow3

--workflow3
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Document without file should fail validation
--workflow3--

###
### STEP 14: Test Pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents?page=1&limit=1

###
### STEP 15: Delete a Document (removes from database, not from Arweave)
### Note: Replace with actual document ID
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/document/REPLACE_WITH_ACTUAL_DOCUMENT_ID

###
### STEP 16: Verify Document is Deleted from Database
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents

###
### STEP 17: Try to Access Deleted Document (should fail)
### Note: Replace with the deleted document ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/document/REPLACE_WITH_DELETED_DOCUMENT_ID

###
### STEP 18: Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout

###
### STEP 19: Try to Access Protected Endpoint After Logout (should fail)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/upload/documents

###
### STEP 20: Try to Login with Wrong Password (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{workflowEmail}}",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}